  "details": "In the current version of VRChat, the bottom left of the screen seems to have a cursor which triggers the Pointer Enter and Pointer Exit events on Event Trigger components.\n\nExample video VR: (The pointer seems to be slightly outside of the FOV, so it's a bit difficult visualize)\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nu8bcsVqj4E\n\nFor reference, this also happens on desktop but will probably cause less issues.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cv1dVWzF_7Q\n\nThe setup looks like the attached screenshot.\n\nThis can be quite a problem for creating UIs that are attached to the left hand. I usually disable hand interactions if the hand pointer is over the UI. However, this issue causes that function to trigger whenever the hand is in the wrong position.\n\nEdit 16.5.2023:\n\nA test world is now available (reset button included)\n\nhttps://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_0d0bd6a8-9508-44a0-a07c-66f121ad8347",
